cool breeze wrote:
>
> I heard this guy Kent Paul Dolan always gets what he calls the
> "protection racket" . As I select only chaotic creatures, my chances
> of getting to minetown at level 1 are very slim.  Is the lack of
> "protection racket" a sufficient reason to never play chaotic
> creatures?

If you read the ascension posts of very successful players you will see
they no longer use the protection racket.  The protection racket is a
strategy to learn how to survive a leel 1 character to mine town.  If
you can not yet survive that descent then it doesn't matter what
alignment you play you stand to gain in skills by trying it in some of
your games.  By the time you can survive more than half of your
characters at level 1 to mine town you are likely to discover it no
longer helps you gain further playing skill.


